            <div xml:id="d561-a1">

                <pb facs="0773" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg667"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Representative Gardner to Mr. Root.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >House of Representatives,<lb/>Committee on Arts and
                                Expositions</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                            C,</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-01-18"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">January 18,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I spoke to you to-day about
                    the appreciation expressed by Gloucester people of the courteous act of
                    Inspector O’Reilly, who by prompt action recovered American fishing gear and
                    fish that would otherwise have been lost in the ice. I quote from a letter just
                    received from William H. Jordan, collector of the port of Gloucester, Mass.:</p>
                <p>“I thought you would be interested in knowing that a letter Mr. Merchant received
                    yesterday from Doctor Webber at Bay of Islands, sent at the request of Captain
                    Ross, stated that Inspector O’Reilly of the Newfoundland cutter <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Fiona</hi> went into Penguin and Goose Arm last Tuesday,
                    which were frozen over, broke up the ice, and recovered all the fishing gear and
                    a large haul of herring that would have been lost except for that act of
                    courtesy on the part of Inspector O’Reilly.”</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. P. Gardner</hi>,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
